WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.653
Hermes stormed back into the banquet room.

2
00:00:04.654 --> 00:00:11.237
"Oops," Brody said. "I guess my plan to lose during the Games isn't going to work."

3
00:00:11.238 --> 00:00:16.662
He felt terrible. He'd wanted to find a way to help Heracles.

4
00:00:16.663 --> 00:00:21.738
Instead Brody had just made things worse for everyone.

5
00:00:21.739 --> 00:00:25.928
"What are we going to do now?" Julia asked.

6
00:00:25.929 --> 00:00:34.657
Markos shook his head. "I don't know. Because if Brody proves to Hermes that he's doing his best by winning one or more events—"

7
00:00:34.658 --> 00:00:39.626
"Then Heracles will end up in Tartarus," Julia finished grimly.

8
00:00:39.627 --> 00:00:47.799
"There's still just one obvious solution," she added. "Heracles has to win everything."

9
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:55.504
"But Julia," Markos started to argue, "if Hermes thinks Brody isn't doing his best—"

10
00:00:55.505 --> 00:01:04.436
"Hermes won't think that," Julia said. "Not if we can stop the other gods from sabotaging Heracles. If

11
00:01:04.437 --> 00:01:13.195
Heracles gets to compete fairly, without any interference from the gods, nobody will be surprised if he wins every event." "Hey!"

12
00:01:13.196 --> 00:01:18.297
Brody protested. "I might win something!" Then

13
00:01:18.298 --> 00:01:25.131
he thought for a second, remembering some of the amazing things he'd seen Heracles do. "Actually,

14
00:01:25.132 --> 00:01:28.943
never mind. I guess you're right." "So

15
00:01:28.944 --> 00:01:36.644
if Brody comes in second in some of the games, Hermes will believe he's doing his best," Julia went on. "That

16
00:01:36.645 --> 00:01:44.423
way Heracles will be safe from Tartarus, and Hermes probably won't even care if we go back through the rift right away." "What

17
00:01:44.424 --> 00:01:49.322
if Zeus decides to kill me or make me his slave?" Brody said. "That

18
00:01:49.323 --> 00:01:52.092
was part of the deal, remember?" "Don't

19
00:01:52.093 --> 00:01:57.663
worry too much about that," Markos said. "I think Julia is right. If

20
00:01:57.664 --> 00:02:04.337
Heracles wins all the events in the Games, Zeus will be busy bragging and strutting around. He

21
00:02:04.338 --> 00:02:07.280
won't pay any attention to you." "We

22
00:02:07.281 --> 00:02:11.507
need to talk to Heracles and Iphicles," Julia said. "We

23
00:02:11.508 --> 00:02:18.641
have to tell them what's going on and ask Iphicles to help us." Then she looked at Markos. "For

24
00:02:18.642 --> 00:02:25.912
now, I have another problem—I have to find another water jar so I can bring home some water." Julia

25
00:02:25.913 --> 00:02:32.719
and Markos headed toward the fountain. Brody followed them, feeling uneasy. What

26
00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.781
if Hermes decided Brody hadn't tried hard enough? What

27
00:02:36.782 --> 00:02:40.760
if the messenger god refused to let them leave? And

28
00:02:40.761 --> 00:02:47.669
how were they supposed to stop the other gods from interfering with Heracles during the Games? Finally Brody

29
00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:52.613
decided to stop worrying about all that stuff. Julia and

30
00:02:52.614 --> 00:02:56.734
Markos were smart—they'd figure everything out. Brody just

31
00:02:56.735 --> 00:03:00.133
had to hold up his end of the deal. That meant

32
00:03:00.134 --> 00:03:08.843
getting some sleep so he could train hard tomorrow! * *

33
00:03:08.844 --> 00:03:17.345
* "Your boxing technique could still use some work, boy," Hermes said the next morning. "Let's find you a sparring

34
00:03:17.346 --> 00:03:25.963
partner." Brody glanced around the gymnasium. Almost all the gods he'd ever seen were there today, along with their

35
00:03:25.964 --> 00:03:31.449
champions. Heracles was nearby, tossing a javelin under Zeus' watchful

36
00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:37.451
eye. "Heracles doesn't look too busy," Brody said. "Should I ask him to spar with

37
00:03:37.452 --> 00:03:45.902
me?" Hermes smiled with approval. "Trying to show me you're sorry by boxing with the toughest competitor out there, eh? I like

38
00:03:45.903 --> 00:03:53.021
it. Go ahead—I'll be right there. I just need to discuss something with

39
00:03:53.022 --> 00:03:56.548
Caerus." Brody hurried over to Zeus and

40
00:03:56.549 --> 00:04:02.600
bowed. "Uh, hi, sir. I was wondering if your champion would spar with me for a

41
00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:10.390
while." Zeus looked amused. "You're Hermes' champion, aren't you, my boy?" he said in his booming

42
00:04:10.391 --> 00:04:14.060
voice. "You can certainly spar with my

43
00:04:14.061 --> 00:04:19.753
champion. Perhaps it's good to experience some humiliation before the Games

44
00:04:19.754 --> 00:04:27.151
begin!" "Yeah. I mean no!" Brody said, flustered for a moment. "Thanks,

45
00:04:27.152 --> 00:04:32.451
Zeus." Soon Brody and Heracles were circling each other, taking jabs now and

46
00:04:32.452 --> 00:04:40.532
then. Brody was pretty sure that Heracles was going easy on him, since only a couple of Heracles' punches hit their marks.

47
00:04:40.533 --> 00:04:46.007
Zeus was watching them, so Brody didn't dare to speak to Heracles for a while.

48
00:04:46.008 --> 00:04:53.039
Finally, though, Athena called to Zeus. The king of the gods went over to talk to her.

49
00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:58.476
"Listen," Brody hissed at Heracles. "I need to tell you something."

50
00:04:58.477 --> 00:05:07.956
As quickly as he could, he whispered everything he knew about the gods' plots against Heracles. Heracles listened, looking worried.

51
00:05:07.957 --> 00:05:12.424
"I know the gods don't play fair, of course," he said when Brody finished.

52
00:05:12.425 --> 00:05:17.088
"And I know that as Zeus' champion, I am a favorite target of the gods.

53
00:05:17.089 --> 00:05:20.211
But I didn't realize it would be this bad."

54
00:05:20.212 --> 00:05:27.115
Brody nodded and dodged a jab. " All the gods are after you," he

55
00:05:27.116 --> 00:05:32.691
said. "Well, except for Zeus, of course. And maybe Athena. But we want to help

56
00:05:32.692 --> 00:05:37.504
you." Now Heracles looked surprised. "How?" he

57
00:05:37.505 --> 00:05:43.917
asked. Brody couldn't resist taking advantage of his opponent's distraction to land a punch on Heracles'

58
00:05:43.918 --> 00:05:50.197
shoulder. The muscles there felt as hard as rocks, and Heracles hardly seemed to notice the

59
00:05:50.198 --> 00:05:57.032
punch. "We have a plan," Brody said. "Well, Julia does. And she's good at that sort of

60
00:05:57.033 --> 00:06:02.738
thing." Once again he spoke quickly, explaining what Julia had in

61
00:06:02.739 --> 00:06:06.789
mind. "You and Julia have been good to me," Heracles

62
00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:10.900
said. "I wish to do whatever I can to help you return to your own

63
00:06:10.901 --> 00:06:14.526
time." One corner of his mouth twitched into a

64
00:06:14.527 --> 00:06:19.041
smile. "And of course I wish to keep myself out of Tartarus." His smile

65
00:06:19.042 --> 00:06:21.451
faded. "Plus, I have to think of my brother."

66
00:06:21.452 --> 00:06:25.085
Brody nodded. "We're hoping Iphicles will help us too.

67
00:06:25.086 --> 00:06:28.924
Julia and Markos are supposed to be talking to him right now."

68
00:06:28.925 --> 00:06:33.331
"I'm sure he will help." Heracles still looked anxious.

69
00:06:33.332 --> 00:06:37.119
"I worry about what could happen to him if I end up disgraced."

70
00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:43.040
"What do you mean?" Brody asked, ducking to avoid another jab.

71
00:06:43.041 --> 00:06:49.466
Heracles sighed. "Iphicles is a fine person," he said.

72
00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:56.469
"But he can be a bit . . . gruff at times. And the gods take offense so easily."

73
00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:01.966
He shook his head, replacing his worried expression with a determined one.

74
00:07:01.967 --> 00:07:05.532
"In any case, my thanks to you and your friends, Brody.

75
00:07:05.533 --> 00:07:13.860
I am with you. Just tell me what you need me to do."

